## What a Private Party Actually Needs

Unlike a wedding or a corporate event, a private party is usually run by the person hosting it, not by an event planner or a stage manager. That changes what the AV setup needs to do. You do not need a technician cueing a lighting plot or riding a mixing desk. You need a system that works the moment our crew leaves, so a host, a friend with the aux cable, or a Bluetooth connected phone can carry the night from there.

The [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) is built around exactly that: 2 high quality active speakers with stands for a playlist or a connected device, 1 wired dynamic microphone for cutting a cake, making a toast or calling out a speech, and 2 RGBW LED light bars for ambient color instead of a bare patio light. Aesthetic cabling and professional setup are included, so nothing looks like a rental once our crew leaves. It is built for villa gardens, private rooms and terraces, up to 50 guests, which is the real ceiling on this package, not a rounded marketing number.

